{"chunk_id": "8e8cc4ef7ab8", "text": "This section marks the formal beginning of the Bhagavad Gita within the Mahabharata. Dhritarashtra asks Sanjaya to describe what happens when the Kauravas and Pandavas assemble on the sacred battlefield of Kurukshetra. Sanjaya recounts how Duryodhana, seeing the well\u2011organized Pandava army, approaches his teacher Drona and lists the powerful warriors on both sides, revealing both confidence and anxiety. The grandsire Bhishma sounds his conch, triggering a thunderous chorus of war instruments from both armies. Krishna and Arjuna answer with their own divine conches. As the battle is about to begin, Arjuna asks Krishna to place his chariot between the armies so he can observe those he must fight. Seeing relatives, teachers, and friends on both sides, Arjuna is overwhelmed with grief and moral doubt, setting the stage for the philosophical dialogue of the Gita.\nAs the Bhagavad Gita begins, Duryodhana surveys the armies, conches sound, and Arjuna asks Krishna to place his chariot between the forces, then falters in grief.\nThemes: battlefield tension, duty vs compassion, family conflict, war ritual, moral crisis", "vector": [4.054993769386783e-05, -0.012150159105658531, -0.008779600262641907, 0.013488964177668095, 0.0027263853698968887, 0.025215279310941696, -0.016711514443159103, 0.0023109521716833115, -0.023492997512221336, -0.020169533789157867, 0.01918729394674301, 0.017935948446393013, -0.010313507169485092, 0.009324540384113789, 0.0017004167893901467, 0.016724970191717148, 0.03156619518995285, -0.004016414750367403, 0.025914957746863365, -0.00997039582580328, -0.013549513183534145, -0.022268563508987427, -0.0008001714013516903, 0.0028962588403373957, -0.01667114906013012, 0.02333153411746025, 0.014006993733346462, -0.015002687461674213, -0.007864637300372124, 0.0069362204521894455, -0.0240850318223238, -0.0037944018840789795, -0.003686759155243635, -0.002936624689027667, -0.010172226466238499, -0.006398007273674011, 8.18